# Setup and import scripts

## Idempotency

- Setup and import scripts must be idempotent: running them more than once must not duplicate master data or break existing records.
- Prefer upsert by natural key (No., Code, Name). If a record exists, update mutable fields; if not, insert.
- Do not delete and recreate company-wide data unless the script is explicitly a reset tool and says so.

## Configuration

- Never hard-code credentials or secrets. Use environment variables from `.env` (see `.env.example`).
- Company ID, tenant, environment, and API base URL come from config — not from literals in script bodies, except documented defaults that are clearly overridable.

## APIs

- Call standard Business Central APIs first.
- Use custom `apex/manufacturing` APIs only for manufacturing entities or actions that standard APIs cannot perform.
